	(text "Isolated interface: digital isolator, set-point DAC, readback ADC"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12 18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 4.0 4.0)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 40 90 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "49aa1a89-2b04-5100-8e70-30782fcd3604")
	)
	(text "SPI crosses the barrier. The DAC and ADC carry their own references, so no precision reference or trimmer is needed."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12 22.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(italic yes)
				(color 70 70 70 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "bd311f4a-58e3-5058-9ac7-0a4733fb9638")
	)
	(text "A   Digital isolator"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.5 33.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 50 120 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5549d879-4e0a-52dc-b9a4-0d93e78fcd11")
	)
	(text "ISOLATION BARRIER"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 80.5 114 90)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
				(color 200 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b5a42e12-5474-5762-91ff-9f1edc1bb479")
	)
	(text "Side 1 = MCU (3.3 V), side 2 = analog (5 V). Five channels go to the analog side, MISO comes back.\nISO7761 (no F suffix) outputs default HIGH when side 1 is unpowered or the input floats: chip selects stay\nde-asserted and LOAD_OFF_ISO is asserted, so the load is OFF until firmware says otherwise. R21-R23 give\nthe same guarantee while the MCU is in reset. Propagation delay 11 ns: keep SPI at or below 2 MHz."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 18 128 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "894303a9-798c-542a-b83e-3ef0a80c8bcf")
	)
	(text "B   Set-point DAC: A = current ceiling, B = CV voltage"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 161.5 33.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 50 120 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f65795b3-c86f-583e-8a44-7f98f16b417c")
	)
	(text "12 bit, internal 2.048 V reference, gain 2: 0 - 4.095 V in 1 mV steps.\nA: LOAD_CTRL, 2.5 A per volt = 2.44 mA per LSB. B: CV_SET in VSEN volts.\nBoth outputs are 0 V after power-up (POR shutdown): no EEPROM surprise like the MCP4725."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 163 92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0a02cff1-29b1-5014-901e-b47737b35fff")
	)
	(text "C   Readback ADC: 16 bit, 4 channels"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 161.5 105.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 50 120 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8f877bf7-299c-5101-8a1e-19e6c66830eb")
	)
	(text "AIN0 ISEN (0.30 V/A), AIN1 VSEN (0.049 V/V), AIN2 heatsink NTC, AIN3 the live V_SET node\n(PGA +-256 mV): shows what the loop really gets after OTP, OFF, KILL or CV pull it down.\nInternal reference 0.01 %, 7 ppm/K, 860 SPS, plus a die temperature sensor."
